# §2. Definitions and special rules

> Module Section2

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using SaraIncome as Inc
> Using SaraPredicates as P
> Using Section7703 as S7703
> Using Section152 as S152

Port of `section2.pl`. §2 defines the two filing statuses §1 needs beyond
"married" and "unmarried": the **surviving spouse** of (a) and the **head of
household** of (b). Both are built out of machinery that already exists here —
kinship windows, §152 dependency, §151 entitlement, and §7703(b)(2)'s
cost-of-maintaining-a-household test — which is why §2 comes last.

`SaraStatus` reads both conclusions from injections today; with this module
they can also be derived.

## Shared shapes

Three window tests recur. The Prolog writes each as a `\+ role_(E,_) ; role_(E,V)`
disjunction, so an event with no date is "no constraint" and an event with
several contributes each of them.

```catala-metadata
## `\+ start_(R,_) ; ( start_(R,S), is_before(S,First) )` and the matching end
## test: a residence that spans the whole taxable year.
declaration spans_year content boolean
  depends on ev content W.Event, y content integer
  equals
    ((number of ev.starts) = 0
     or (exists s among ev.starts such that s <= (W.first_day_year of y)))
    and ((number of ev.ends) = 0
         or (exists e among ev.ends such that (W.last_day_year of y) <= e))

## As above but requiring an actual start date, which several paragraphs do by
## writing `start_(R,S)` outside the disjunction.
declaration starts_before_year content boolean
  depends on ev content W.Event, y content integer
  equals exists s among ev.starts such that s <= (W.first_day_year of y)

## A `nonresident_alien_` event that overlaps the taxable year at all.
declaration nra_in_year content boolean
  depends on ev content W.Event, y content integer
  equals
    ((number of ev.starts) = 0
     or (exists s among ev.starts such that s <= (W.last_day_year of y)))
    and ((number of ev.ends) = 0
         or (exists e among ev.ends such that (W.first_day_year of y) <= e))

## A kinship window that covers the whole taxable year, with `var(...)` read as
## "no constraint" on that end.
declaration window_covers content boolean
  depends on w content K.Window, y content integer
  equals
    (match w.starts_on with pattern
     -- Absent: true
     -- Present content s: s <= (W.first_day_year of y))
    and (match w.ends_on with pattern
         -- Absent: true
         -- Present content e: (W.last_day_year of y) <= e)

## The residences at a household, and the people living in them.
declaration residents_at content list of W.Entity
  depends on world content W.World, household content W.Entity
  equals
    combine all ag
      among (map each ev among
              (list of e among world.events
               such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                         and e.patients contains household)
             to ev.agents)
      in acc initially []
      with acc ++ ag

declaration households_of content list of W.Entity
  depends on world content W.World, taxpayer content W.Entity
  equals
    combine all ps
      among (map each ev among
              (list of e among world.events
               such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                         and e.agents contains taxpayer)
             to ev.patients)
      in acc initially []
      with acc ++ ps
```

## (a)(1)(A) The spouse died in one of the two preceding years

```catala-metadata
declaration scope SpouseDiedRecently:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## the marriages the taxpayer is an agent of
  output candidates content list of S7703.Candidate
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope SpouseDiedRecently:
  definition candidates equals
    (output of S7703.MaritalStatusA with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).candidates

  definition holds equals
    exists c among candidates such that
      (exists ms among c.marriage.starts such that
         (exists dv among world.events such that
            dv.kinds contains W.EventKind.Death
            and dv.agents contains c.spouse
            and (exists td among dv.starts such that
                   ms <= td
                   # the marriage was not already over when the spouse died
                   and ((number of c.marriage.ends) = 0
                        or (exists me among c.marriage.ends such that td <= me))
                   # ... during either of the two preceding years
                   and (W.first_day_year of (taxable_year - 2)) <= td
                   and td <= (W.last_day_year of (taxable_year - 1)))))
```

## (a)(1)(B) Maintains a home for a child

Both the taxpayer's and the dependant's residence must span the whole year, the
taxpayer must furnish over half the cost — §7703(b)(2) — and the dependant must
be the taxpayer's child (or the taxpayer their stepparent) throughout, with a
§151(c) entitlement.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope MaintainsHomeForChild:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output households content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope MaintainsHomeForChild:
  definition households equals households_of of world, taxpayer

  definition holds equals
    exists h among households such that
      # the taxpayer's own residence spans the year and has a start date
      (exists rt among
        (list of e among world.events
         such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                   and e.agents contains taxpayer
                   and e.patients contains h)
       such that (starts_before_year of rt, taxable_year)
                 and (spans_year of rt, taxable_year))
      and (output of S7703.LivingApartTwo with {
             -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- household: h
             -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
      and (exists dep among (residents_at of world, h) such that
             (exists rd among
               (list of e among world.events
                such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                          and e.agents contains dep
                          and e.patients contains h)
              such that (starts_before_year of rd, taxable_year)
                        and (spans_year of rd, taxable_year))
             and (exists w among
                   ((K.windows_between of child_of, dep, taxpayer)
                    ++ (K.windows_between of stepparent_of, taxpayer, dep))
                  such that window_covers of w, taxable_year)
             and ((W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s151_c_applies_3,
                     [taxpayer.id; dep.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])
                  or (output of S152.IsDependent with {
                        -- injections: injections -- world: world
                        -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                        -- taxpayer_generated: false
                        -- dependant_generated: false
                        -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                        -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                        -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                        -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                        -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
                        -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
                        -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
                        -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds))
```

## (a)(2) Limitations

(A) the taxpayer remarried before the close of the year; (B) *unless* a joint
return could have been made for the year the spouse died, which fails only when
either was a nonresident alien.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Remarried:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output marriages content list of W.Event
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope JointReturnPossible:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input spouse content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope Remarried:
  definition marriages equals
    list of e among world.events
    such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
              and e.agents contains taxpayer

  ## Two distinct marriages of the taxpayer, the later one starting on or
  ## before the close of the taxable year.
  definition holds equals
    exists prev among marriages such that
      (exists re among marriages such that
         re.ident.id != prev.ident.id
         and (exists ps among prev.starts such that
                (exists rs among re.starts such that
                   ps <= rs and rs <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))))

scope JointReturnPossible:
  ## `s2_a_2_B(bob,Spouse,2014)` is asked with `Spouse` unbound, and the test
  ## is inside a negation: `agent_(Someone_is_nra,Spouse)` then unifies with
  ## *any* agent, so an unbound spouse makes every nonresident-alien event
  ## count, not none. That is the mode, not a shortcut.
  definition holds equals
    not (exists ev among world.events such that
           ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.NonresidentAlien
           and (ev.agents contains taxpayer
                or (match spouse with pattern
                    -- Absent: (number of ev.agents) > 0
                    -- Present content sp: ev.agents contains sp))
           and (nra_in_year of ev, taxable_year))
```

## (a) Surviving spouse

```catala-metadata
declaration scope SurvivingSpouse:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output clause_a content boolean
  output clause_b content boolean
  output limited content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope SurvivingSpouse:
  definition clause_a equals
    (output of SpouseDiedRecently with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds

  definition clause_b equals
    (output of MaintainsHomeForChild with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds

  ## `s2_a_2` is `s2_a_2_A ; \+ s2_a_2_B` — note the negation on (B).
  definition limited equals
    (output of Remarried with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
    or not (output of JointReturnPossible with {
              -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
              -- spouse: (output of S7703.MaritalStatusA with {
                            -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                            -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).spouse
              -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds

  definition holds equals clause_a and clause_b and not limited

  exception definition holds
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s2_a_3,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true
```

## (b)(2) Determination of status

(A) legal separation, which is `Section7703.LegalSeparation` on the marriage
itself; (B) a nonresident-alien spouse; (C) a spouse who died during the year.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope SpouseNonresidentAlien:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input spouse content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope LegallySeparatedFrom:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input spouse content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope SpouseDiedInYear:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input spouse content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope SpouseNonresidentAlien:
  definition holds equals
    exists m among world.events such that
      m.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
      and m.agents contains taxpayer
      # No `sp.id != taxpayer.id` here, deliberately. §7703(a)(1) writes
      # `Taxp\==Spouse` and this provision does not:
      #
      #     s2_b_2_B(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy) :-
      #         marriage_(Marriage),
      #         agent_(Marriage,Taxp),
      #         agent_(Marriage,Spouse),      % no distinctness guard
      #
      # so on a marriage naming a single agent, SARA lets the taxpayer be
      # their own nonresident-alien spouse and (b)(2)(B) holds. Requiring the
      # two to differ is a tidier rule than the one enacted, and it made the
      # port disagree on a four-fact world.
      and (exists sp among m.agents such that
             (match spouse with pattern
                  -- Absent: true
                  -- Present content s: s.id = sp.id)
             and (exists ev among world.events such that
                    ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.NonresidentAlien
                    and ev.agents contains sp
                    and (nra_in_year of ev, taxable_year)))

scope LegallySeparatedFrom:
  definition holds equals
    exists m among world.events such that
      m.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
      and m.agents contains taxpayer
      and m.agents contains spouse
      and taxpayer.id != spouse.id
      and (output of S7703.LegalSeparation with {
             -- world: world -- marriage: m
             -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).separated

scope SpouseDiedInYear:
  definition holds equals
    exists m among world.events such that
      m.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
      and m.agents contains taxpayer
      # `agent_(Marriage,Taxp), agent_(Marriage,Spouse)` with no disequality
      # between them, so on a marriage naming a single agent the taxpayer is
      # their own spouse and their own death ends it. D16 removed this same
      # guard from §2(b)(2)(B) and left (C) alone, on the grounds that (C) is
      # only ever reached with a bound, distinct spouse. The fuzzer reaches it
      # with the spouse unbound.
      and (exists sp among m.agents such that
             (match spouse with pattern
              -- Absent: true
              -- Present content s: s.id = sp.id)
             and not (output of SpouseNonresidentAlien with {
                        -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                        -- spouse: Present content sp
                        -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
             and (exists dv among world.events such that
                    dv.kinds contains W.EventKind.Death
                    and dv.agents contains sp
                    and (exists td among dv.starts such that
                           ((number of m.ends) = 0
                            or (exists me among m.ends such that td <= me))
                           and (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= td
                           and td <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))))
```

## (b)(1) The married test

`s2_b_1` opens with a negation covering a whole marriage: the taxpayer is *not*
married at the close of the year unless some marriage survives all of the
conditions inside it. (b)(2)(A)–(C) are folded in here, which is what the
comment in `section2.pl` means by "s2_b_2 was incorporated directly into
s2_b_1".

```catala-metadata
declaration scope MarriedAtClose:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope MarriedAtClose:
  definition holds equals
    exists m among world.events such that
      m.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
      and m.agents contains taxpayer
      and (exists sp among m.agents such that
             sp.id != taxpayer.id
             and (exists ms among m.starts such that
                    ms <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
             and (if (exists dv among world.events such that
                        dv.kinds contains W.EventKind.Death
                        and dv.agents contains sp)
                  then
                    # the spouse died: during the year, or after its close
                    ((output of SpouseDiedInYear with {
                        -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                        -- spouse: Present content sp
                        -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
                     or (exists dv among world.events such that
                           dv.kinds contains W.EventKind.Death
                           and dv.agents contains sp
                           and (exists td among dv.starts such that
                                  (W.last_day_year of taxable_year) <= td)))
                  else
                    # the spouse did not die: the marriage must run past the
                    # close of the year, or have no end at all
                    ((number of m.ends) = 0
                     or (exists me among m.ends such that
                           (W.first_day_year of (taxable_year + 1)) <= me)))
             and not (output of S7703.LegalSeparation with {
                        -- world: world -- marriage: m
                        -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).separated
             and not (output of SpouseNonresidentAlien with {
                        -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                        -- spouse: Present content sp
                        -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds)
```

## (b)(1)(A)(i) and (ii) — who the household is maintained for

(i) a §152(c) qualifying child, unless that child is both married at the close
of the year and not the taxpayer's dependent by reason of §152(b)(2). (ii) any
other §152 dependent the taxpayer is entitled to a §151 deduction for.

Both are asked with the *taxpayer* unbound — `s2_b_1_A_i(_,charlie,2018)` —
so both quantify over candidate taxpayers the way §152(d)(1)(D) does.

```catala-metadata
## s2_b_1_A_i_I(Dependent,Taxy) — `s7703(Dependent,_,_,Taxy)`, in full.
declaration scope DependentMarried:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input dependant content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  output holds content boolean

## s2_b_1_A_i_II(Dependent,Taxp,Taxy) — `s152_b_2(Dependent,_,Taxp,Taxy)`,
## where the third argument is the *spouse*, not the taxpayer.
declaration scope DependentJointReturnWith:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input dependant content W.Entity
  input spouse content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope QualifyingChildClause:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input dependant content W.Entity
  input taxpayer content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  output candidates content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope OtherDependentClause:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input dependant content W.Entity
  input taxpayer content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output candidates content list of W.Entity
  ## Was the taxpayer bound in the goal? It selects which §152 mode applies.
  output taxpayer_given content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope DependentMarried:
  definition holds equals
    (output of S7703.MaritalStatus with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: dependant
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- qualifying_dependants:
            (output of S152.QualifyingChildrenOf with {
               -- injections: injections -- world: world
               -- taxpayer: dependant -- taxable_year: taxable_year
               -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
               -- descendent_of: descendent_of
               -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).children }).married

scope DependentJointReturnWith:
  ## s152_b_2/4 granted by the case.
  definition holds equals
    (exists m among world.events such that
       m.kinds contains W.EventKind.Marriage
       and m.agents contains dependant
       and m.agents contains spouse)
    and (exists ev among world.events such that
           ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.JointReturn
           and ev.agents contains dependant
           and ev.agents contains spouse
           and ev.starts contains (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)
           and ev.ends contains (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))

  exception definition holds
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s152_b_2_4,
         [dependant.id; -1; spouse.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true

scope QualifyingChildClause:
  definition candidates equals
    match taxpayer with pattern
    -- Present content t: [t]
    -- Absent:
        map each k among (child_of ++ sibling_of ++ stepsibling_of) to k.object

  definition holds equals
    exists t among candidates such that
      (output of S152.QualifyingChild with {
         -- injections: injections -- world: world
         -- dependant: dependant -- taxpayer: t
         -- taxable_year: taxable_year
         -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
         -- descendent_of: descendent_of
         -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).holds_c
      and not ((output of DependentMarried with {
                  -- injections: injections -- world: world
                  -- dependant: dependant -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                  -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                  -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                  -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).holds
               and (output of DependentJointReturnWith with {
                      -- injections: injections -- world: world
                      -- dependant: dependant
                      -- spouse: t
                      -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds)

scope OtherDependentClause:
  definition taxpayer_given equals
    match taxpayer with pattern
    -- Present content tp: true
    -- Absent: false

  # With the taxpayer unbound this is `s152_a(Dep,Taxp,Taxy,_,_)` generating its
  # own taxpayers, and §152(d)(2) reaches in both directions: (C) makes a person
  # the dependent of their own descendant, (D) and (G) route through relations
  # none of these three lists holds. Same universe as `S152.DependantsOf` --
  # everyone the event base names in a role -- with `IsDependent` filtering.
  # D18 was this same mistake one level down; `QualifyingChildClause` keeps the
  # narrow list, because §152(c)(2) really does start at one of those three.
  definition candidates equals
    match taxpayer with pattern
    -- Present content t: [t]
    -- Absent:
        list of e among
          (S152.dedup_people of
            (combine all r
               among (map each ev among world.events
                      to (ev.agents ++ ev.patients))
               in acc initially [] with acc ++ r))
        such that e.id != dependant.id

  # Which §152 mode this is depends on how the goal was asked. With the
  # taxpayer bound, SARA reaches `\+ s152_b_1(Taxp,_,Taxy)` with it bound and
  # the eligibility guard runs. With it unbound the guard is reached before
  # `s152_a` binds anything, so it never runs — D7 — and the port must skip it
  # too, or it denies a taxpayer SARA allows.
  definition holds equals
    exists t among candidates such that
      (let d equals
         (output of S152.IsDependent with {
            -- injections: injections -- world: world
            -- dependant: dependant -- taxpayer: t
            -- taxpayer_generated: (not taxpayer_given)
            -- dependant_generated: false
            -- taxable_year: taxable_year
            -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
            -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
            -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
            -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
            -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
            -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }) in
       (if taxpayer_given then d.holds else d.holds_any_taxpayer)
       # The second conjunct is `s151_b_applies(Taxp,Dep,Taxy) ;
       # s151_c_applies(Taxp,Dep,Taxy)`, and `s151_c_applies` is *defined* as
       # `s152(Dep,Taxp,Taxy)`. That looks like the conjunct just proved, and
       # the port therefore read it as `true` — but it is not the same
       # question. The first conjunct ran with the taxpayer unbound, where D7's
       # ordering skips the eligibility guard; by the time this one is reached
       # the taxpayer is bound and the guard applies. It can and does fail:
       # a taxpayer who is themselves somebody's dependent is found by the
       # first conjunct and rejected by the second.
       and (d.holds
            or (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s151_b_applies_3,
                  [t.id; dependant.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])
            or (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s151_c_applies_3,
                  [t.id; dependant.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])))
```

## (b)(1)(A) and (b)(1)(B) — the two households

(A) is the taxpayer's own home, occupied for more than half the year by
somebody under (i) or (ii). (B) is a household — not necessarily the
taxpayer's — that is a parent's principal place of abode, where §151(c) gives
the taxpayer a deduction for that parent.

The duration test in (A) measures the *residence*, not its overlap with the
taxable year: `duration(Start_individual_residence,End_individual_residence,D)`
with no clipping. The port measures the same span.

```catala-metadata
## §2(b)(3)(B) asks the mirror-image question of `window_covers`: is there a
## relationship whose window had *already run out* by the close of the taxable
## year? `is_before(End_relationship,Last_day)` puts the end on or before the
## last day, and an unbound end -- a relationship the case gave no end date --
## satisfies the `var/1` branch instead.
## A query argument Prolog may leave unbound.
declaration ent_matches content boolean
  depends on want content optional of W.Entity, got content W.Entity
  equals
    match want with pattern
    -- Absent: true
    -- Present content e: e.id = got.id

declaration window_lapsed content boolean
  depends on w content K.Window, y content integer
  equals
    (match w.starts_on with pattern
     -- Absent: true
     -- Present content s: s <= (W.first_day_year of y))
    and (match w.ends_on with pattern
         -- Absent: true
         -- Present content e: e <= (W.last_day_year of y))

declaration scope HouseholdForDependent:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output households content list of W.Entity
  ## The people (b)(1) binds as the dependant, which (b)(3) re-examines.
  output dependants content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope HouseholdForParent:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output households content list of W.Entity
  ## The people (b)(1) binds as the dependant, which (b)(3) re-examines.
  output dependants content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope HouseholdForDependent:
  definition households equals households_of of world, taxpayer

  # `s2_b_1_A` *binds* `Dependent`, and `s2_b` then puts that same person
  # through (b)(3). Reporting only "somebody qualifies" loses the identity, and
  # with it the ability to ask (b)(3)(B) about the right person.
  definition dependants equals
    combine all ds
      among (map each h among
              (list of x among households such that
                 (exists rt among
                   (list of e among world.events
                    such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                              and e.agents contains taxpayer
                              and e.patients contains x)
                  such that
                    # the taxpayer's home: `->` on both dates, so the first of
                    # each is used
                    (match (List.first_element of rt.starts) with pattern
                     -- Absent: true
                     -- Present content st: st <= (W.first_day_year of taxable_year))
                    and (match (List.first_element of rt.ends) with pattern
                         -- Absent: true
                         -- Present content en:
                             (W.last_day_year of taxable_year) <= en))
                 and (output of S7703.LivingApartTwo with {
                        -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- household: x
                        -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds)
             to (list of dep among (residents_at of world, h) such that
                   (exists rd among
                     (list of e among world.events
                      such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                                and e.agents contains dep
                                and e.patients contains h)
                    such that
                      (let s equals
                         (match (List.first_element of rd.starts) with pattern
                          -- Absent: W.first_day_year of taxable_year
                          -- Present content d: d) in
                       let e equals
                         (match (List.first_element of rd.ends) with pattern
                          -- Absent: W.last_day_year of taxable_year
                          -- Present content d: d) in
                       (e - s) * 2 >= ((W.last_day_year of taxable_year)
                                       - (W.first_day_year of taxable_year))))
                   and ((output of QualifyingChildClause with {
                           -- injections: injections -- world: world
                           -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: Present content taxpayer
                           -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                           -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                           -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                           -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).holds
                        or (output of OtherDependentClause with {
                              -- injections: injections -- world: world
                              -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: Present content taxpayer
                              -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                              -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                              -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                              -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                              -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
                              -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
                              -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
                              -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds)))
      in acc initially [] with acc ++ ds

  definition holds equals (number of dependants) > 0

scope HouseholdForParent:
  ## (B) generates the household from the *parent's* residence, not the
  ## taxpayer's, so every household in the world is a candidate.
  definition households equals
    combine all ps
      among (map each ev among
              (list of e among world.events
               such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence)
             to ev.patients)
      in acc initially []
      with acc ++ ps

  definition dependants equals
    combine all ds
      among (map each h among
              (list of x among households such that
                 (output of S7703.LivingApartTwo with {
                    -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- household: x
                    -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds)
             to (list of dep among (residents_at of world, h) such that
                   (exists rp among
                     (list of e among world.events
                      such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                                and e.agents contains dep
                                and e.patients contains h)
                    such that (starts_before_year of rp, taxable_year)
                              and ((number of rp.ends) = 0
                                   or (exists en among rp.ends such that
                                         (W.last_day_year of taxable_year) <= en)))
                   and (exists w among (K.windows_between of child_of, taxpayer, dep)
                        such that window_covers of w, taxable_year)
                   # `s151_c(Taxp,Dep,Deduction,Taxy)` with `Deduction` unbound
                   # -- which is the only mode it is ever called in.
                   # `s151_c/4` is `s151_c_applies/3` and then `s151_d/3`, and
                   # `s151_d` is *total*: it yields 0 under (d)(2)/(d)(5) and
                   # 2,000 otherwise, so with the amount unbound it can only
                   # succeed. The §151(d) half therefore contributes nothing
                   # here, and dropping it is behaviour-preserving rather than
                   # a deviation. It is also what breaks the §68(b) → §2(b) →
                   # §151(c) → §151(d)(3) → §68(b) cycle; SARA's own author
                   # left `s151_c_applies` commented out at section2.pl:310.
                   and ((W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s151_c_applies_3,
                           [taxpayer.id; dep.id; W.num_key of taxable_year])
                        or (output of S152.IsDependent with {
                              -- injections: injections -- world: world
                              -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                              -- taxpayer_generated: false
                              -- dependant_generated: false
                              -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                              -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                              -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                              -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                              -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
                              -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
                              -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
                              -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds)))
      in acc initially [] with acc ++ ds

  definition holds equals (number of dependants) > 0
```

## (b)(3) Limitations, and (b) itself

Two people are barred from heading a household: a nonresident alien, and a
taxpayer whose only dependant is somebody living with them but not related to
them at all — §152(d)(2)(H) alone is not enough.

The second bar is about a *person*, and `s2_b(Taxp,Dependent,Taxy)` puts the
same dependant through (b)(1) and (b)(3). Reporting (b)(1) as a bare boolean
would let one person satisfy (b)(1) while another trips (b)(3); the two scopes
above therefore report which people they bound, and (b) below quantifies over
them jointly.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope NonresidentAlienTaxpayer:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope HouseholdMemberOnly:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input dependant content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output candidates content list of W.Entity
  ## Did the goal name the dependant? It decides which reading of
  ## §152(d)(1)(B) applies.
  output dependant_given content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope NonresidentAlienTaxpayer:
  definition holds equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.NonresidentAlien
      and ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and (((number of ev.starts) = 0
            and ((number of ev.ends) = 0
                 or (exists e among ev.ends such that
                       (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= e)))
           or ((exists s among ev.starts such that
                  s <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
               and ((number of ev.ends) = 0
                    or (exists e among ev.ends such that
                          (W.last_day_year of taxable_year) <= e))))

scope HouseholdMemberOnly:
  definition dependant_given equals
    match dependant with pattern
    -- Present content dp: true
    -- Absent: false

  definition candidates equals
    match dependant with pattern
    -- Present content d: [d]
    -- Absent:
        (combine all ps
           among (map each ev among
                   (list of e among world.events
                    such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.Residence
                              and e.agents contains taxpayer)
                  to (residents_at of world, ev.ident))
           in acc initially []
           with acc ++ ps)
        ++ (map each k among
             (child_of ++ sibling_of ++ descendent_of ++ stepsibling_of)
            to k.subject)
        # `s152_d_2_H(Dependent,Taxp,Taxy,_,StartH,EndH)` is where SARA *binds*
        # the dependant, and a case that grants (H) supplies rows the event
        # base does not. Without them a world whose only content is the grant
        # offers no candidate at all, and §2(b)(3)(B) came out false on a
        # dependant SARA finds.
        ++ (list of e among
              (map each inj among
                 (W.injections_for of injections, P.pred_s152_d_2_H_6,
                    [-1; taxpayer.id; W.num_key of taxable_year; -1; -1; -1])
               to (match (W.injection_entity of inj, 1) with pattern
                   -- Absent: taxpayer
                   -- Present content d: d))
            such that e.id != taxpayer.id)

  definition holds equals
    exists dep among candidates such that
      # \+ s152_b(Dependent,Taxp,Taxy)
      (not ((output of S152.Ineligible with {
               -- injections: injections -- world: world
               -- person: taxpayer -- taxable_year: taxable_year
               -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
               -- descendent_of: descendent_of
               -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
               -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
               -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
               -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
               -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds
            or (output of S152.MarriedDependent with {
                  -- injections: injections -- world: world -- dependant: dep -- spouse: Absent
                  -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds))
      # \+ s152_a_1(Dependent,Taxp,Taxy)
      and not (output of S152.QualifyingChild with {
                 -- injections: injections -- world: world
                 -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                 -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                 -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                 -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                 -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).holds_c
      # s152_d_1_B and s152_d_1_D
      # `s152_d_1_B(Dependent,Taxy)` runs *before* `s152_d_2_H` binds the
      # dependant, so when the goal left it unbound this is the world-wide sum
      # and not a test of `dep` -- one person's income defeats it for everybody.
      and (output of S152.NoIncome with {
             -- world: world -- injections: injections -- dependant: dep
             -- dependant_unbound: (not dependant_given)
             -- taxable_year: taxable_year
             -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
             -- descendent_of: descendent_of
             -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).holds
      and not (output of S152.AnyQualifyingChildTaxpayer with {
                 -- injections: injections -- world: world
                 -- dependant: dep -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                 -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                 -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                 -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of }).holds
      # ... and no relationship under (A)-(G) that had lapsed by year end
      and (let qr equals
             (output of S152.QualifyingRelativeRelationship with {
                -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                -- windows_h: []
                -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
                -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
                -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
                -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }) in
           not (exists w among qr.windows
                such that window_lapsed of w, taxable_year))
      # ... but (H) does hold, across the whole year
      and (exists w among
            (output of S152.MemberOfHousehold with {
               -- injections: injections -- world: world
               -- dependant: dep -- taxpayer: taxpayer
               -- taxpayer_generated: false
               -- dependant_generated: (not dependant_given)
               -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).windows
           such that window_covers of w, taxable_year)
```

## (b)(1) and (b) — head of household

```catala-metadata
declaration scope HeadOfHouseholdOne:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output married content boolean
  output surviving_spouse content boolean
  output clause_a content boolean
  output clause_b content boolean
  ## The people (A) and (B) bind as `Dependent`, which (b)(3) re-examines.
  output dependants content list of W.Entity
  output holds content boolean

declaration scope HeadOfHousehold:
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input dependant content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input child_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  input stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  input child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  input sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  ## s2_b_3/3
  output limited content boolean
  output holds content boolean
```

```catala
scope HeadOfHouseholdOne:
  definition married equals
    (output of MarriedAtClose with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds

  definition surviving_spouse equals
    (output of SurvivingSpouse with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds

  definition clause_a equals
    (output of HouseholdForDependent with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds

  definition clause_b equals
    (output of HouseholdForParent with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds

  definition dependants equals
    if married or surviving_spouse then []
    else
      (output of HouseholdForDependent with {
         -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
         -- taxable_year: taxable_year
         -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
         -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
         -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
         -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
         -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
         -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).dependants
      ++ (output of HouseholdForParent with {
            -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
            -- taxable_year: taxable_year
            -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
            -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
            -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
            -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
            -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
            -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).dependants

  definition holds equals
    (not married) and (not surviving_spouse) and (clause_a or clause_b)

scope HeadOfHousehold:
  ## `s2_b_3/3` for the dependant the caller named, where they named one.
  definition limited equals
    (output of NonresidentAlienTaxpayer with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
    or (output of HouseholdMemberOnly with {
          -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
          -- dependant: dependant -- taxable_year: taxable_year
          -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
          -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
          -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
          -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
          -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
          -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds

  ## `s2_b(Taxp,Dependent,Taxy) :- s2_b_1(Taxp,_,Dependent,Taxy),
  ## \+ s2_b_3(Taxp,Dependent,Taxy)` -- one dependant has to clear *both*, so
  ## the quantifier is over the people (b)(1) bound, not over the two tests
  ## independently.
  definition holds equals
    not (output of NonresidentAlienTaxpayer with {
           -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
           -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).holds
    and (exists dep among
           (output of HeadOfHouseholdOne with {
              -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
              -- taxable_year: taxable_year
              -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
              -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
              -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
              -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
              -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
              -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).dependants
         such that
           (ent_matches of dependant, dep)
           and not (output of HouseholdMemberOnly with {
                      -- injections: injections -- world: world
                      -- taxpayer: taxpayer
                      -- dependant: Present content dep
                      -- taxable_year: taxable_year
                      -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
                      -- descendent_of: descendent_of
                      -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
                      -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
                      -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
                      -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
                      -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds)

  exception definition holds
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s2_b_3,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true
```
